From 92cc9f6f15eaa03e47c98dc775d5cdce26c14dc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: swsammy <g.0gn15@passmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:51:04 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] brw: Prevent late cmod propagation into SIMD32
 three-source instructions

Before Gfx12, SIMD32 three-source instructions must not have condition
modifiers. Width lowering already enforces this restriction, but the cmod
propagation passes after scheduling can add a condition modifier after
width lowering has run. No later pass splits the resulting instruction.

This produces mad.l.f0.0(32) with FP16 operands and Align16 encoding in
ncnn shaders requiring subgroup size 32. On Comet Lake and Whiskey Lake,
these shaders hang the GPU and cause VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST.

Reject propagation into three-source instructions wider than SIMD16 before
Gfx12 once the shader reaches AFTER_EARLY_LOWERING. Earlier propagation
remains allowed so width lowering can handle it. Add regression tests and
an instruction-validator check for the forbidden combination.

No shader-db changes on Skylake or Ice Lake.

Fixes: b967942b642 ("brw: Do cmod prop again after scheduling")
Fixes: 09450faf6a1 ("brw: Do cmod prop again after post-RA scheduling")
Closes: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/issues/16526
Generated-by: LLM
