From f9d7a5b88c3cb0ef85b30d301414add9f607c635 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: swsammy <g.0gn15@passmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:51:04 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] brw: Limit Gfx9 three-source instructions to SIMD16

On Comet Lake and Whiskey Lake, SIMD32 Align16 FP16 three-source
instructions use the execution-mask bit of lane L - 8 for lanes 16..31.
Under non-uniform control flow, this leaves some active lanes unwritten
and writes some inactive lanes, producing incorrect ncnn inference
results. The behaviour is reproducible on Mesa 25.3.6 as well as main.

This is measured hardware behaviour rather than a documented restriction.
The pre-Gfx8 workaround in elk_fs.cpp describes a related eight-channel
shift per compressed half. Intel's Windows driver emits paired SIMD16
MAD instructions for the tested shader even at required subgroup size 32.

Cap three-source instructions at SIMD16 on Gfx9, the only platform using
Align16 three-source encoding in brw. Add width-lowering regression tests
and reject SIMD32 Gfx9 three-source instructions in the validator. The
standalone reproducer passes at subgroup sizes 16 and 32 with the fix.

Although the measurements cover only fp16 on two Gfx9 parts, deliberately
cap all three-source instructions at SIMD16 on all Gfx9 devices,
including NoMask instructions. With the hardware behaviour undocumented,
conservatively applying the restriction to the whole instruction class
and generation is the safer choice. The practical impact is limited to
16-bit types: fp32 and fp64 three-source instructions are already split
by the two-register rule.

No shader-db changes on Skylake or Ice Lake.

Backport-to: 26.1
Closes: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/issues/16528
Generated-by: LLM
